# taskforge-tui — EAV port (apps/taskforge-tui, semsc v0.1).
#
# FULL 1:1 port of the 24-operation heap-array terminal todo app: the keyboard
# reader, ANSI screen control, the bounded C-string/JSON buffer helpers, the
# fixed-offset JSON tokenizer, the table renderer + edit modal, scroll/selection
# math, JSON load/save, the todo-array mutators, and the interactive `main`
# state machine. Every c.* / pointer.* / math.* call is converted; the imperative
# mutable-state machine is expressed with the EAV `set` step (README §12).
#
# Execution is deferred: the keyboard adapter (`c.terminalReadKey`) and the
# interactive REPL loop have no headless runtime, so the app parses + lints clean
# as `target console` but is not run by the suite. File I/O (c.fopen/fgets/…) is
# real libc; only the terminal-input + interactive loop gate execution. (X-042)
#
# Conversions / language differences:
#   - `storage local …` → `let`; `storage module …` → module `storage` entities.
#   - `set memory X V` → the `set X V` step (the §12 mutable-assignment step the
#     port exercise motivated; counter rebinds from a call result use the call's
#     `out` instead).
#   - inline `call`/`argument`/`run`/`bind value` → first-class `call` entities
#     with `arg`/`out`; `ignore value source … type T` → `discards`.
#   - `authority ACTION PATH` → covering `capability`/`grants` + `uses` (§8).
#   - `EnumName.equal` domain method → `compare.equalInt32` (EAV enums are i32
#     discriminants).
#   - `branch if condition C target L` → `branch if C goto L`; `branch else
#     target L` / `jump target L` → `goto L`; `label L` → `at L`.
#   - main returns `ExitCode` (console-entry ABI), so the v0.1 `Result ExitCode
#     MainError` + `makeError`/`return error` become a nonzero exit code, and
#     malloc failure is detected with `pointer.isNull` (uniform with the file
#     open it already null-checks) — `CAllocationError`/`MainError` are dropped.
#   - the handle-less `defer … showCursor (deferRunOn all)` becomes a targeted
#     `showCursor` on the quit path (the only path that hid the cursor); EAV
#     cleanups are handle-scoped (`cleans <handle>` required).

TaskforgeTui is project
TaskforgeTui module appTaskforgeTui
TaskforgeTui target console
TaskforgeTui entry main

appTaskforgeTui is module
appTaskforgeTui path apps.taskforgeTui
appTaskforgeTui exports main
appTaskforgeTui exports readTuiKey
appTaskforgeTui exports renderScreen
appTaskforgeTui exports loadTodosFromJson
appTaskforgeTui exports saveTodosToJson
appTaskforgeTui purpose "Keyboard-driven console todo app with heap-backed storage and JSON persistence"
appTaskforgeTui invariant "main.sem owns the TUI lifecycle, keyboard handling, in-memory todo arrays, and todos.json load/save"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32
ExitCode purpose "Process exit status"

TuiKeyCode is alias
TuiKeyCode for Int32
TuiKeyCode purpose "A raw console byte (0..255) or a normalized TUI key (>255)"

SaveTodosStatus is enum
SaveTodosStatus variant SaveSucceeded
SaveTodosStatus variant SaveOpenFailed
SaveTodosStatus variant SaveWriteFailed
SaveTodosStatus variant SaveCloseFailed
SaveTodosStatus purpose "Outcome of a saveTodosToJson attempt"

ScreenMode is enum
ScreenMode variant ListMode
ScreenMode variant EditMode
ScreenMode purpose "Whether the TUI is in the list view or the edit modal"

consoleStdinReader is capability
consoleStdinReader grants read console.stdin
consoleStdinReader purpose "Authority to read one no-echo console key"

consoleStdoutWriter is capability
consoleStdoutWriter grants write console.stdout
consoleStdoutWriter purpose "Authority to write ANSI control sequences and table rows"

memoryBufferReader is capability
memoryBufferReader grants read memory.buffer
memoryBufferReader purpose "Authority to read heap-backed title/edit/line buffers"

memoryBufferWriter is capability
memoryBufferWriter grants write memory.buffer
memoryBufferWriter purpose "Authority to write heap-backed title/edit buffers"

filesystemReader is capability
filesystemReader grants read filesystem
